@format 1
@id project.restore-session
@title Restore session
@area 7. Project persistence
@entry input
@summary Recreate the visible session while durable relay plans continue to use their own stable stage identities and snapshots.
@section II. Functionality
@flow TB
@related preview.open-media, project.save-session
@tag session
@tag restore

@alias window = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainWindow.PWindow
@alias scene = Cadroue.Infrastructure.LScene
@alias courier = Cadroue.UIShell.PMainArea.LCourier

[input] Main window is created <input>
- Choose default tabs or the last saved session from preferences @ window.PWindowTabsRestore(...)
> tabs

[tabs] Restore tabs <process>
- Create each saved tab with its output preset and layout record @ window.PWindowSceneRestore(...)
- Restore custom tab names @ window.PWindowSceneRestore(...)
- Restore relay slots and resolve funnel targets @ window.PWindowSceneRestore(...)
- Select the saved active tab index @ window.PWindowSceneRestore(...)
! Restored tab GUIDs are display identities only; unfinished saved plans resolve stable stage IDs through the courier.
> media

[media] Restore optional media <decision>
- Check the open-last-media preference and saved path @ window.PWindowMediaRestore(...)
? "Saved media exists and automatic restore is enabled" > open
? "Media restore is disabled or unavailable" > result

[open] Continue with media open <output>
> map:preview.open-media

[result] Session restored <output>
= Tabs reflect the saved session, while previously submitted relay routes remain authoritative in their durable batch plans.
